  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.8.0 introduces compositor-driven streaming reveal transitions for incremental Markdown updates, along with a new streaming playground in the desktop demo.\n\n## Highlights\n\n### Streaming reveal transitions\n* Smoothly animate newly appended Markdown text and fenced code blocks during streaming updates via `CompositionCustomVisualHandler`, running off the UI thread and returning settled lines to static drawing as soon as each transition finishes.\n* Choose between two reveal modes via `MarkdownStreamingRevealMode`:\n  * `Character` — uniformly fades in each newly streamed text chunk while gently rising newly appearing lines (leaving settled prefixes on the same line aligned).\n  * `Line` — fades in and gently rises each newly appearing visual line.\n* Tune fade and vertical rise independently with inherited properties (`StreamingRevealDuration`, `StreamingRevealRiseDuration`, and `StreamingRevealOffset`) on `MarkdownRenderer` or individual `MarkdownTextBlock` controls.\n* Full document loads render immediately without animation, text selection completes active transitions cleanly, and reflow, theme/foreground updates, inline code pills, text decorations, and bidirectional/CJK text are handled seamlessly.\n\n### Desktop demo\n* Added a **Streaming** sample (`Streaming.md`) with live controls to switch reveal modes, adjust fade duration, rise duration, and vertical rise offset, and replay the stream.\n\n### Other\n* Fixed a missing XML documentation comment in `LiveMarkdown.Avalonia.Svg`.\n\n---\n\n## Usage\n\nEnable streaming reveal on `MarkdownRenderer` (properties are inherited by nested `MarkdownTextBlock` and `CodeBlock` instances):\n\n```xml\n<md:MarkdownRenderer\n    MarkdownBuilder=\"{Binding MarkdownBuilder}\"\n    StreamingRevealMode=\"Character\"\n    StreamingRevealDuration=\"0:0:0.220\"\n    StreamingRevealRiseDuration=\"0:0:0.380\"\n    StreamingRevealOffset=\"4\" />\n```\n\nOr configure it in code:\n\n```csharp\nrenderer.StreamingRevealMode = MarkdownStreamingRevealMode.Character; // None (default) | Line | Character\nrenderer.StreamingRevealDuration = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(220);    // Fade-in duration (0 skips fading)\nrenderer.StreamingRevealRiseDuration = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(380);// Rise duration for new lines\nrenderer.StreamingRevealOffset = 4;                                   // Vertical rise in DIPs (0 disables rising)\n```\n\n> **Note:** Reveal animations trigger on incremental updates (such as appending to `MarkdownBuilder` / `ObservableStringBuilder`). Replacing the full document renders immediately.\n\n---\n\n## Compatibility\nStreaming reveal is opt-in (`StreamingRevealMode` defaults to `None`), introduces no breaking API changes, and remains compatible with Avalonia `12.0.0` with no additional package dependencies.\n\n**Full Changelog:** [v2.7.0...v2.8.0](https://github.com/DearVa/LiveMarkdown.Avalonia/compare/v2.7.0...v2.8.0)\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/DearVa/LiveMarkdown.Avalonia/compare/v2.7.0...v2.8.0",
